_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.4.1 RC1 \n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.rc1 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - Radeon RX 560 Series (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 31.0.21912.14) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-4570 CPU @ 3.20GHz (4 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nI noticed that if we edit code and we have hidden tile editors, they constantly become visible, i.e. they expand.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/31f002c4-9f95-45e0-8a7d-cd0cdd1df6f4\n\nI also see this error all the time when this problem happens:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1cc190c0-b8b4-4c26-aa01-e9b70dafe774)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a TileMapLayer\n2. Attach a script to it\n3. Make sure the TileMapLayer is selected, has a TileSet, and has tile editors at the bottom\n4. Indent the code or select the randomize() function from the tooltip\n5. This will open the tile editor, although we don't need it\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nI usually attach the MRP, but it's very easy to do following the instructions above.","closed_by":{"login":"JekSun97","id":130399274,"node_id":"U_kgDOB8W8Kg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130399274?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97","html_url":"https://github.com/JekSun97","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/events{/pr